From: WP1 Audio (Agent 3) <audio@rg35xxh.local>
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] jive_alsa: clamp absurd buffer/period params
Upstream: squeezeplay@758bc11 src/squeezeplay/src/audio/decode/decode_alsa_backend.c
Proposed-As: audio/alsa/proposals/0002-clamp-absurd-buffer-params.patch
Reviewed-By: Squeezebox RG35XX H Agent 2 (Core), WP2
Rationale: USEALSABUFFERTIME/USEALSAPERIODCOUNT accept any positive value:
 buffer_time=1 (1 us) yields an XRUN storm, buffer_time=10000000 pins 10 s
 of latency, period_count=1 starves the autostart gate. Clamp to sane
 bounds with a visible warning instead of silently misbehaving.
Review: fields are unsigned int (%u correct); LOG_WARN macro flavor matches
 this TU (no category arg). Placed after the mandatory-arg usage check and
 after the period_count>100 cpu-randomisation fold in -p parsing, so the
 >100 escape hatch keeps working. Clamp targets (30000 us, 3 periods)
 equal ALSA_DEFAULT_BUFFER_TIME/PERIOD_COUNT in decode_alsa.c. Bounds
 5..500 ms / 2..16 cover every real device; fail-soft, no new exit path.
Apply: patch -p1 < 0005-jive-alsa-clamp-buffer-params.patch (from upstream repo root)
---

diff --git a/src/squeezeplay/src/audio/decode/decode_alsa_backend.c b/src/squeezeplay/src/audio/decode/decode_alsa_backend.c
--- a/src/squeezeplay/src/audio/decode/decode_alsa_backend.c
+++ b/src/squeezeplay/src/audio/decode/decode_alsa_backend.c
@@ -1398,6 +1398,20 @@ int main(int argv, char **argc)
 		exit(-1);
 	}

+	/* Fail-soft bounds: 5..500 ms buffer, 2..16 periods. */
+	if (state.buffer_time < 5000 || state.buffer_time > 500000) {
+		LOG_WARN("buffer_time %u us out of range, clamping to 30000",
+			 state.buffer_time);
+		state.buffer_time = 30000;
+	}
+	if (state.period_count < 2 || state.period_count > 16) {
+		/* NB: period_count > 100 enables cpu randomisation above and
+		 * is already folded back into range before we get here. */
+		LOG_WARN("period_count %u out of range, clamping to 3",
+			 state.period_count);
+		state.period_count = 3;
+	}
+
 	if(!state.pcm_wait_timeout) {
 		state.pcm_wait_timeout = PCM_WAIT_TIMEOUT;
 	}
